DESCRIPTION:
  Config-file-gated command injection in tinyhttpd with snprintf buffering and
  config-gated strict sanitization. Config file enables the exec gate; cmd flows
  through snprintf into system(). Strict metachar check only activates with
  --strict-exec; without it the check is skipped and exploitation works.

CONFIG_GATE (C2 — config file):
  mechanism:  read_exec_config() populates exec_cfg via fopen/fgets/sscanf;
              exec_cfg.enabled && exec_cfg.logging guard in accept_request()
  check:      two-field struct guard before dispatch
  complexity: file I/O → struct → two-field guard

  CONFIG FILE:
    --config /path/to/file
    File format:
      exec_mode = 1
      exec_logging = 1

INPUT_FLOW (I2 — buffered):
  path:       handle_exec() → snprintf(shell_cmd, ..., "sh -c '%s' 2>/dev/null",
              cmd) → system(shell_cmd)
  transforms: one snprintf buffer

SANITIZATION (S3 — config-gated strict filter):
  check:      static int strict_exec = 0; set by --strict-exec
              if (strict_exec && strpbrk(cmd, "|;&`$") != NULL) reject 403
  bypass:     omit --strict-exec; strict_exec=0, check never evaluated

SINK:        system(shell_cmd) via snprintf in handle_exec()

CHANGED FILES:
  httpd.c — 4 hunks: struct + strict_exec global + send_exec_reply +
    read_exec_config + handle_exec (I2 S3) + accept_request intercept +
    main() with --port/--config/--strict-exec parsing

